{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1505720-a-kind-of-nosferatu","id":1505720,"title":"A kind of Nosferatu","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-18T17:19:47-07:00","id":1505720,"title":"A kind of Nosferatu","content":"Look, I know this may sound a little strange and maybe even stupid, but have you ever had the experience of playing with a Nosferatu that uses obfuscate to look like a beautiful person, of course there must be someone who used it to hunt, but I mean using it constantly just to walk down the street and feel good about itself or feel like somehow normal, it's something I think would be an interesting concept, but I never see anyone using it, the closest I've seen it is an NPC who died like a dog.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T17:27:01-07:00","id":1505722,"title":"","content":"My experience is with Requiem, but I imagine someone else at least thought of this.<br /> <br /> Thing is, there must be a catch or almost every Nosferatu would be making themselves look at least normal, if not beautiful. Maybe keeping the illusion requires constant concentration or blood expenditure (thus requiring more hunting). Or, if the power you're using is like the Familiar Stranger, it could backfire at unexpected moments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T17:32:10-07:00","id":1505724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1505720-a-kind-of-nosferatu?p=1505722#post1505722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My experience is with Requiem, but I imagine someone else at least thought of this.<br /> <br /> Thing is, there must be a catch or almost every Nosferatu would be making themselves look at least normal, if not beautiful. Maybe keeping the illusion requires constant concentration or blood expenditure (thus requiring more hunting). Or, if the power you're using is like the Familiar Stranger, it could backfire at unexpected moments.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I'm not mistaken, the problem here is not blood, but the fact that the illusion is broken if someone touches you and you wouldn't necessarily be hidden from cameras, more than that I think it's due to the successes or part of the narrator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T17:49:28-07:00","id":1505730,"title":"","content":"Well, <i>there's</i> your problem.<br /> <br /> You make yourself look beautiful, someone's going to want to touch you. Maybe you meet someone you <i>want</i> to touch yourself, and you've used Obfuscate for so long you don't even think about it anymore... <i>Until</i> contact is made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T17:55:14-07:00","id":1505732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1505720-a-kind-of-nosferatu?p=1505730#post1505730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, <i>there's</i> your problem.<br /> <br /> You make yourself look beautiful, someone's going to want to touch you. Maybe you meet someone you <i>want</i> to touch yourself, and you've used Obfuscate for so long you don't even think about it anymore... <i>Until</i> contact is made.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I don't mean using it lightly either, but I mean using it in controlled environments, like at a night club or a private party, an exhibition, any kindred that lets its guard down that much deserves destruction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T18:22:26-07:00","id":1505737,"title":"","content":"Everyone lets their guard down, sooner or later. It might only be for a second, or a microsecond, but that may be all it takes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T18:52:39-07:00","id":1505743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1505720-a-kind-of-nosferatu?p=1505737#post1505737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone lets their guard down, sooner or later. It might only be for a second, or a microsecond, but that may be all it takes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-19T03:21:43-07:00","id":1505771,"title":"","content":"It's IIRC totally noted as a thing that happens, particularly among younger Nosferatu. Some use their powers to assume false identities basically full-time, although it's a bad idea.<br /> <br /> This might be part of the reason Nosferatu discourage a reliance on Obfuscate. Your disguise or invisibility is going to break eventually and when it does you'd better be ready to get out of there and drop a trail using entirely mundane means. It might be tonight or it might be the 29th April 2138ce, but it's going to happen.<br /> <br /> On the flip side there are certainly Nossies who use makeup and Obfuscate to play up their monstrosity, particularly around other kindred. With a bit of care they'll unsettle even the most unflappable Ventrue.<br /> <br /> Requiem Nossies find it easier than Masquerade Nossies simply because they rarely have the 'deformed limbs and foot thick scar tissue' look.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-19T10:26:21-07:00","id":1505789,"title":"","content":"I do like the Nosferatu of the Reqium myself in that setting along with Gangrel and Mekhet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-19T10:33:53-07:00","id":1505793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1505720-a-kind-of-nosferatu?p=1505789#post1505789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do like the Nosferatu of the Reqium myself in that setting along with Gangrel and Mekhet.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the difference?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-19T10:43:22-07:00","id":1505795,"title":"","content":"The Nosferatu in VTR are not always physically deformed. In fact many of them look normal but give of a sense of unease or a predatory sense of interaction. Some of them become very emotionally detached and cold and there clan book goes into further detail on how the curse separates them from humanity and Kindred.<br /> <br /> I even had a notion of one kind of Nosferatu who physical flaws would go away with each passing century and would look inhumanly perfect just like the flaw in the Aberrant 1st edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 03-19-2023, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-19T14:12:19-07:00","id":1505812,"title":"","content":"On this subject a player came to me with a proposed merit called &quot;monstrous beauty&quot; for pc. Nossie starts as app 0 as usual and can never pass as humour but can buy dots in appearance. Sort of inverted rugged bad looks. About 5 points.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-19T14:17:23-07:00","id":1505817,"title":"","content":"Interesting idea Ragged Robin. Any ideas what kind of flaw would offset the bonus such a merit would give.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-19T14:22:58-07:00","id":1505820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1505720-a-kind-of-nosferatu?p=1505812#post1505812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On this subject a player came to me with a proposed merit called &quot;monstrous beauty&quot; for pc. Nossie starts as app 0 as usual and can never pass as humour but can buy dots in appearance. Sort of inverted rugged bad looks. About 5 points.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you should use this concept to make a strangely beautiful new clan using this concept rather than applying it to Nosferatu, I mean, I think it does away with the concept of being a Nosferatu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-19T14:45:23-07:00","id":1505824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1505720-a-kind-of-nosferatu?p=1505817#post1505817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting idea Ragged Robin. Any ideas what kind of flaw would offset the bonus such a merit would give.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> you'd never pass as human so parts of the flaw would still be intact. You'd also be expected to buy the appearance dots in game which is a big points pit for something only circumstantially useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T17:26:14-07:00","id":1506386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1505720-a-kind-of-nosferatu#post1505720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, I know this may sound a little strange and maybe even stupid, but have you ever had the experience of playing with a Nosferatu that uses obfuscate to look like a beautiful person, of course there must be someone who used it to hunt, but I mean using it constantly just to walk down the street and feel good about itself or feel like somehow normal, it's something I think would be an interesting concept, but I never see anyone using it, the closest I've seen it is an NPC who died like a dog.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm unfamiliar with V20 or 5th edition, but in 1st, 2nd, and Revised, this was pretty easy to do. As written, it was impossible for mortals to penetrate Obfuscate. (The sole exception was the suggestion that people with certain psychic abilities may be able to challenge it similarly to the way vampires with Auspex were able to, and that very young children may be able to see through the illusion.) Once an Obfuscate power is activated, it requires little to no effort to maintain, and only ends when the user makes a conscious choice to end it (or the scene ends). <br /> <br /> Mask of A Thousand Faces never says anything about human contact*. The biggest issue was trying to imitate a specific person, as it required studying the subject. Trying to imitate your former self it easier, as you aren't trying to mimic another person's behavior or knowledge. But because Nosferatu don't have to spend character dots on Appearance, any character with primary Socials is going to have at least a 4 or 5 in Manipulation for the Manipulation + Acting/Performance (difficulty 7) roll to craft a mask. <br /> <br /> There's a premade character template in the revised clan book called The Skin who specializes in impersonating people. (For some reason - the writer or developer - the character only has 2 in Obfuscate. Meanwhile, there's a version of the Cleopatra template who has Obfuscate 3, but specifically mentions having refused to learn how to make herself look human again. Go figure.) <br /> <br /> *(As far as touching someone using Mask of a Thousand Faces, my own take is that because Unseen Presence specifically mentions that people will instinctively avoid the user while walking or moving, anyone touching the user of MoaTF will subconsciously ignore any discrepancies between the visual appearance and tactile sensation.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T18:17:40-07:00","id":1506391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1505720-a-kind-of-nosferatu?p=1506386#post1506386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm unfamiliar with V20 or 5th edition, but in 1st, 2nd, and Revised, this was pretty easy to do. As written, it was impossible for mortals to penetrate Obfuscate. (The sole exception was the suggestion that people with certain psychic abilities may be able to challenge it similarly to the way vampires with Auspex were able to, and that very young children may be able to see through the illusion.) Once an Obfuscate power is activated, it requires little to no effort to maintain, and only ends when the user makes a conscious choice to end it (or the scene ends).<br /> <br /> Mask of A Thousand Faces never says anything about human contact*. The biggest issue was trying to imitate a specific person, as it required studying the subject. Trying to imitate your former self it easier, as you aren't trying to mimic another person's behavior or knowledge. But because Nosferatu don't have to spend character dots on Appearance, any character with primary Socials is going to have at least a 4 or 5 in Manipulation for the Manipulation + Acting/Performance (difficulty 7) roll to craft a mask.<br /> <br /> There's a premade character template in the revised clan book called The Skin who specializes in impersonating people. (For some reason - the writer or developer - the character only has 2 in Obfuscate. Meanwhile, there's a version of the Cleopatra template who has Obfuscate 3, but specifically mentions having refused to learn how to make herself look human again. Go figure.)<br /> <br /> *(As far as touching someone using Mask of a Thousand Faces, my own take is that because Unseen Presence specifically mentions that people will instinctively avoid the user while walking or moving, anyone touching the user of MoaTF will subconsciously ignore any discrepancies between the visual appearance and tactile sensation.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I played a version with the house rules based on the A20 version, it wasn't very specific, maybe I'm just used to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}